# Entry Main: `call(C)` and `call(code := C)` in a value context are the call of C and return its result (the book
# #structural-call, #return-in-data; step 21.7 K3). The forms of the receiver, the reading of one Structure and its
# ambiguity are those of the statement. r 7, s 7.
int: r 0
int: s 0
D:
    return: int
    C:
        return: 7
---
Main:
    node\r := call(D\C)
    node\s := call(code := D\C)
